  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1241 PM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nMid and upper level ridging will be in place Wednesday, with the\nflow aloft gradually transitioning to southwesterly on Thursday\nand Friday. Meanwhile, the low-level winds will become\nsoutheasterly, leading to temperatures trending upward with highs\nmostly in the 70s and lows in the 50s. As mentioned in the\nprevious discussion, our region will remain between the active jet\npattern, with the polar jet over the central and high plains and\nthe subtropical jet over northern Mexico into deep south Texas. We\nshould see enough moisture and subtle lift to result in some low\n(20-40%) chances for precipitation beginning late Saturday night\nand continuing through early next week. Rain chances still appear\nto be favored on Sunday with a weak cold front moving into the\nregion. We don't expect to see a significant cool-down behind the\nfront, but temperatures should ease back closer to climatological\nnormals.",
